        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "80a6a5cd-48aa-5792-b784-580d74f47f1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Tull, Todd Phillips, Daniel Goldberg, Jon Lucas, Scott Moore, Lawrence Sher\n- Companies: Legendary Entertainment, Warner Bros., Universal Studios\n- Films: The Hangover, Garden State, The Dictator\n- Places: Las Vegas\n- Concepts: bachelor party, cinematography, film production\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Tull was born in 1970 and is an American businessman and film producer.\n- Lawrence Sher was born on February 4, 1970 and is an American cinematographer and film director.\n- Legendary Entertainment was founded by Thomas Tull in 2000.\n- In 2005, Legendary Entertainment concluded an agreement with Warner Bros. to co-produce and co-finance films.\n- The Hangover is a 2009 American comedy film directed by Todd Phillips, co-produced with Daniel Goldberg, and written by Jon Lucas and Scott Moore.\n- The Hangover tells the story of Phil Wenneck, Stu Price, Alan Garner, and Doug Billings traveling to Las Vegas for a bachelor party to celebrate Doug Billings's impending marriage.\n- Lawrence Sher is best known for comedy films such as Garden State, The Hangover, and The Dictator.\n- In 2014, Legendary Entertainment began a similar co-production arrangement with Universal Studios.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
